{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_042 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.7150 acc, a large jump over config_002 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.6287, showing scvi_n200 is a far stronger RNA representation. However, we have only one scvi_n200 experiment and cannot yet attribute the gain to the RNA encoder alone versus the multimodal combination. With pca_n2000, RNA-only was 0.5907 vs multimodal 0.6287 (image added ~3.8 pp). Question: Does the image modality still contribute meaningful value when paired with the much stronger scvi_n200 encoder? config_010 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) isolates this by removing the image modality while keeping everything else aligned with config_042. Why best next experiment: It is a single-variable ablation of the current best configuration, directly reducing uncertainty about whether multimodal fusion is necessary or whether scvi_n200 alone drives the performance. This determines whether remaining budget should target multimodal refinements (fusion, aggregation) or RNA-encoder variants, making it the highest-information-per-experiment choice under a limited budget."
}

